---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PaintCalculator from '../../components/PaintCalculator.astro';
import { webApplicationSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/schema';
import { CALCULATORS_HUB } from '../../data/tools';

const path = '/calculators/paint-calculator';
const title = 'Paint Calculator: Gallons for Rooms & Walls';
const description =
  'Estimate how much paint you need for rooms, individual walls, or a known area. Adjust coats and coverage, subtract openings, and estimate ceiling paint separately.';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: CALCULATORS_HUB.title, href: '/calculators' },
  { label: 'Paint Calculator' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  schema={[
    webApplicationSchema({
      name: 'Paint Calculator',
      description,
      path,
    }),
    breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  ]}
>
  <div class="container-site container-calc calc-page">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

    <header class="calc-page__intro">
      <h1 class="section-heading">Paint Calculator</h1>
      <p class="section-lede calc-page__lede">
        Estimate wall paint in gallons for a room, individual walls, or a known area. Adjust coats and coverage to
        match your product, optionally subtract openings, and estimate ceiling paint as a separate line.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="calc-page__tool">
      <PaintCalculator />
    </div>

    <p class="calc-page__disclaimer">
      This calculator estimates paint quantity from the dimensions, coats, and coverage rate you enter. Actual
      coverage varies by paint product, surface texture and porosity, application method, color change, and other
      conditions. Check the product label or technical data before purchasing. This tool does not determine coating
      compatibility, hazardous-surface preparation, ventilation, or professional coating specifications.
    </p>

    <article class="prose-article calc-page__copy">
      <h2>How the paint calculation works</h2>
      <p>
        For a rectangular room, wall area is 2 × (length + width) × wall height. Optional openings are subtracted to
        get paintable wall area. That area is multiplied by the number of coats, then divided by your coverage rate
        (sq ft per gallon per coat) to get calculated gallons. Purchase quantity rounds that value up to whole US
        gallons. Ceiling paint, when enabled, uses the room’s length × width and its own coats and coverage — it is
        never merged into the wall gallon total.
      </p>

      <h2>How many square feet does a gallon of paint cover?</h2>
      <p>
        Coverage depends on the product and surface. Sherwin-Williams commonly cites about 350–400 sq ft per gallon for
        typical interior paint. Some Behr products list broader ranges such as about 250–400 sq ft per gallon. Benjamin
        Moore lines often list higher figures on technical data (for example around 400–450 sq ft/gal for some interior
        paints). This calculator defaults to 350 sq ft/gal as a conservative planning value — edit it to match the
        label or technical data for the paint you plan to use. Coverage is not universal.
      </p>

      <h2>How many coats of paint do you need?</h2>
      <p>
        The calculator defaults to two coats as a planning value. Benjamin Moore’s paint calculator assumes two coats,
        and Benjamin Moore product guidance often recommends two top coats for optimal hide and color development.
        One coat may be enough for some same-color repaints; dramatic color changes or porous surfaces may need more.
        Follow your product instructions and surface conditions.
      </p>

      <h2>Should you subtract doors and windows?</h2>
      <p>
        Subtracting openings is optional and off by default. Exact measured opening area is best when you have it —
        use Custom area. Count mode uses approximate Benjamin Moore estimating allowances of 20 sq ft per door and 15
        sq ft per window. Those are planning allowances, not measured dimensions for every opening.
      </p>

      <h2>How much ceiling paint do you need?</h2>
      <p>
        In Room mode you can estimate ceiling paint separately. Ceiling area is length × width. Ceiling coats and
        coverage are editable and independent from wall settings because ceiling paint is often a different product or
        color.
      </p>

      <h2>How much extra paint should you buy?</h2>
      <p>
        This calculator does not add a percentage overage. Calculated gallons are rounded up to whole gallons for
        purchase planning. Leftover paint is often kept for touch-ups when labeled and stored properly. Package options
        (quarts, gallons, 5-gallon containers) vary by product and retailer — this tool does not optimize packages.
      </p>

      <h2>Example calculations</h2>
      <h3>10 × 12 ft room, 8 ft walls, 2 coats, 350 sq ft/gal, no openings</h3>
      <p>
        Gross wall area = 352 sq ft. Coat-adjusted demand = 704 sq ft. Calculated ≈ 2.01 gal → purchase 3 gallons.
      </p>
      <h3>Same room with 1 door and 2 windows (count method)</h3>
      <p>
        Deduction = 20 + 15 + 15 = 50 sq ft. Paintable = 302 sq ft. With 2 coats at 350 sq ft/gal ≈ 1.73 gal → purchase
        2 gallons.
      </p>
      <h3>Ceiling only for that room</h3>
      <p>
        Ceiling area = 120 sq ft. Two coats at 350 sq ft/gal ≈ 0.69 gal → purchase 1 gallon of ceiling paint, separate
        from walls.
      </p>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>How much paint do I need?</h3>
      <p>
        Multiply paintable area by coats, divide by coverage per gallon, then round up to whole gallons for purchase.
      </p>
      <h3>How many square feet does a gallon cover?</h3>
      <p>
        Check your product. Many interior latex products fall roughly in the 300–400+ sq ft/gal range on smooth
        surfaces. This tool defaults to 350 and lets you edit.
      </p>
      <h3>How much paint for a 10×12 room?</h3>
      <p>
        With 8 ft walls, no openings, 2 coats, and 350 sq ft/gal, expect about 2.01 calculated gallons (buy 3). Openings
        and different coverage change the result.
      </p>
      <h3>Do I need two coats?</h3>
      <p>
        Two coats are a common planning default and match many manufacturer recommendations for full color development,
        but your project may differ. Choose coats in the calculator.
      </p>
      <h3>Should I subtract windows and doors?</h3>
      <p>
        Optional. Use measured opening area when possible, or approximate counts of 20 sq ft per door and 15 sq ft per
        window.
      </p>
      <h3>How much ceiling paint do I need?</h3>
      <p>
        Ceiling area is length × width. Estimate it separately with its own coats and coverage in Room mode.
      </p>
      <h3>Does this include primer?</h3>
      <p>
        No. Primer is a separate product with its own coverage. Estimate primer separately if your project needs it.
      </p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.sherwin-williams.com/en-us/color/color-tools/paint-calculator" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Sherwin-Williams — Paint Calculator FAQ
          </a>
          — typical gallon coverage about 350–400 sq ft
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.benjaminmoore.com/en-us/paint-calculator" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Benjamin Moore — Paint Calculator
          </a>
          — assumes two coats; does not include ceiling
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://media.benjaminmoore.com/WebServices/prod/assets/production/datasheets/TDS_0549/N549_TDS_US.pdf"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Benjamin Moore — Regal Select technical data
          </a>
          — example interior coverage 400–450 sq ft/gal; recommends two coats for full color development
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.benjaminmoore.com/en-us/paint-calculator" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Benjamin Moore estimating guidance (door/window allowances)
          </a>
          — approximate 20 sq ft per door and 15 sq ft per window used in estimating practice with BM calculators
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.behr.com/how-to/interior/determine-how-much-interior-paint-to-buy" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Behr — How much interior paint to buy
          </a>
          — some products cite about 250–400 sq ft/gal per coat
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .calc-page__copy :where(h2, h3) {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
